  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-08-30T23:55:41.565Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I'd like to request a feature that I believe a lot of people would benefit greatly from, especially those who show up in populated lobbies and encounter lots of familiar people. The feature would be a simple button that resets all of your manually shown avatars, and a separate button that resets all of your manually hidden avatars. Any custom overrides you had for specific people would be reset to use your current safety settings.\nThese two buttons would fit perfectly into the performance options in the safety tab of the menu, or it could go in the advanced settings menu inside the settings tab, along with the \"clear cache\" and \"clear local data\" buttons. \nThis feature would greatly benefit anyone who frequents the same VRChat worlds, encounters the same people often, or simply does not have a powerful system to manage loaded avatars. Generally, when I encounter people I haven't met in VRChat before, I tend to show their avatar manually when having a conversation, or if I had just sent a friend request to them, the safety settings do not update until they change avatars so I generally will show their avatar manually at that point as well. The show avatar button is a great feature that allows you to pinpoint certain people and show them without having to drastically alter your safety settings, however, when I show people manually, it does not reset until I select that specific person again to reset their settings. This can be problematic if you've shown a lot of your friends' avatars and end up in a world with a lot of them at once. If your computer isn't powerful enough, it can drastically hinder performance, and at worst, it could crash your game.\nAs someone who attends a lot of events hosted by community members like music venues or community meetups, it is extremely common for me to end up in a place where I have manually shown up to 20, even 30 people at one time. This tends to happen often when going to these events because you will show people like event hosts, performers, or simply people you've encountered for the first time, and then you will either encounter similar people at other events, or you show up to that same event on another night and encounter new hosts, performers, and people, prompting you to show more avatars. It is extremely inconvenient to manually reset everyone's individual settings, and it is even harder when you're battling 4 frames per second because your PC cannot handle everyone's avatars at once.\nAdditionally, with new features such as Hiding avatars based on distance, it would give this feature even more purpose. With the additional option \"allow override with Show Avatar\" being implemented, this can render the intended performance boost nearly useless. My experience in the beta using this feature at events has been generally good, but mixed when using this specific option because I'd like to use it to show specific people like a DJ or a host that would ruin immersion if their avatar disappeared at a distance, but enabling the override causes me to show nearly half the lobby because of all the people I have manually shown. Having the reset would be great for other things like hiding everyone other than pinpointed friends that would otherwise be extremely inconvenient resetting everyone's overrides manually.\nThank you all for hearing me out, I think this feature would find great use for the game, and I hope it can be implemented soon to improve everyone's experience in the long run!\n-Dova",
